meta {
  name: Create unit
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/curricula/{{curriculumId}}/nodes
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "unit",
    "title": "Number system",
    "sequence": 1,
    "description": "Whole numbers, factors and multiples."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.kind: eq unit
  res.body.curriculum_id: eq {{curriculumId}}
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setEnvVar("curriculumUnitId", res.body.id);
}

docs {
  Nodes are the syllabus points content gets mapped to. The tree is unit,
  chapter, topic, and it is a tree rather than a list because that is how
  teachers talk about a syllabus and how content lines up with it: a book
  covers a unit, a worksheet covers one topic in it.

  curriculum_id comes from the path and is refused in the body with 422.
  Sending both invites them to differ, and a node under the wrong syllabus is
  invisible in the one it was meant for.

  sequence is the order it is taught in, not an id. It is not required to be
  unique -- two topics can be taught in the same week -- so the list falls back
  to creation order when they tie.
}
